{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing a stitch task (#5483) to implement srd073-printf requirements R3.1-R3.4 in the go-unix-utils project. The task requires:\n   - Implementing R3.1 (C-style escape sequences in FORMAT: \\\\, \\a, \\b, \\f, \\n, \\r, \\t, \\v, \\NNN, \\xHH, \\uHHHH, \\UHHHHHHHH)\n   - Implementing R3.2 (argument recycling: reuse format when more args remain)\n   - Implementing R3.3 (missing arguments: use 0 for numeric, \"\" for string)\n   - Implementing R3.4 (quote-prefixed numeric args: '\"A' → 65)\n   - Adding differential tests for each R3 requirement\n   - Ensuring `go build`, `go test`, and `go vet` all pass\n   - Following the execution constitution (no git commands, SPDX headers, function ≤40 lines, etc.)\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern using `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` comparing Go binary vs `gprintf` reference binary\n   - SIGPIPE handler via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Printf format string parsing with escape sequences, conversion specifiers, width/precision\n   - Argument recycling loop in `runPrintf`\n   - Quote-prefix character value parsing ('\"A' → int64(65))\n   - `LC_ALL=C` environment for all test cases\n   - Stderr normalization (`gprintf:` → `printf:`) for error message comparison\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd073-printf.yaml**\n     - Source of truth for all requirements. R3 section (lines 43-53) specifies escape sequences, argument recycling, missing argument defaults, and quote-prefix numeric parsing.\n     - Non-goals: No %q, no --help/--version as flags.\n\n   - **cmd/printf/main.go** (404 lines, existing implementation)\n     - Header: `// Implements srd073-printf R1.1-R1.4, R2.1